  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Campus Sexual Harassment Prevention Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supports efforts to combat sexual harassment at the University of Eswatini, grossly affecting women and marginalized groups. This project seeks to engage 1200 students in advocacy, education, and positive norm-building. Activities of this quarter include the commemoration of the international movement against Gender Based Violence and awareness campaigns. The project aims to foster a safer campus environment and empower students as advocates for change. It aligns with SDG 5 (Gender Equality) and national efforts to combat gender-based violence in Eswatini.</narrative>
  </description>
